  "title": "George Harrison – songs, albums, biography, photos and more!",
  "date": null,
  "content": "<div class=\"breadcrumbs\" typeof=\"BreadcrumbList\" vocab=\"https://schema.org/\">\n<span property=\"itemListElement\" typeof=\"ListItem\"><a property=\"item\" typeof=\"WebPage\" title=\"Go to Beatle people.\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/\" class=\"post post-page\"><span property=\"name\">Beatle people</span></a><meta property=\"position\" content=\"1\"></span> » <span property=\"itemListElement\" typeof=\"ListItem\"><span property=\"name\" class=\"post post-page current-item\">George Harrison</span><meta property=\"url\" content=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/george-harrison/\"><meta property=\"position\" content=\"2\"></span></div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><blockquote><div>Everybody dreams of being famous, rich and famous. Once you get rich and famous, you think, ‘This wasn’t it.’ And that made me go on to find out what it is. In the end, you’re trying to find God. That’s the result of not being satisfied. And it doesn’t matter how much money, or property, or whatever you’ve got, unless you’re happy in your heart, then that’s it. And unfortunately, you can never gain perfect happiness unless you’ve got that state of consciousness that enables that.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">George Harrison</div><p></p><div class=\"content-column one_third\"><div id=\"Index_Harrison_1\" class=\"widgets_on_page wop_tiny1  wop_small1  wop_medium1  wop_large1  wop_wide1\"><ul></ul></div></div><div class=\"content-column one_third\"><div id=\"Index_Harrison_2\" class=\"widgets_on_page wop_tiny1  wop_small1  wop_medium1  wop_large1  wop_wide1\"><ul></ul></div></div><div class=\"content-column one_third\"><div id=\"Index_Harrison_3\" class=\"widgets_on_page wop_tiny1  wop_small1  wop_medium1  wop_large1  wop_wide1\"><ul></ul></div></div><div style=\"clear: both;\"></div><p></p><div id=\"mediavine-settings\" data-blocklist-content-desktop=\"1\"></div></div><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Published:</strong> <time itemprop=\"datePublished\" datetime=\"2008-03-14T15:30:02+00:00\" content=\"2008-03-14T15:30:02+00:00\">14 March 2008 </time> | <time itemprop=\"dateModified\" datetime=\"2025-09-05T17:43:46+01:00\" content=\"2025-09-05T17:43:46+01:00\"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 5 September 2025</time></div><h2>Biography</h2><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></span> <a href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <a href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/3/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></a> <a href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/4/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></a></div><p>George Harrison was lead guitarist, songwriter and singer with The Beatles. Although often overshadowed by the partnership of <a href=\"#/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a> and <a href=\"#/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a> during the band&#8217;s lifetime, he emerged as a significant talent in his own right. <span id=\"more-12\"></span></p><div id=\"ez-toc-container\" class=\"ez-toc-v2_0_89 ez-toc-wrap-right counter-hierarchy ez-toc-counter ez-toc-grey ez-toc-container-direction\"><div class=\"ez-toc-title-container\"><p class=\"ez-toc-title\" style=\"cursor:inherit\">Contents</p>\n<span class=\"ez-toc-title-toggle\"><a href=\"#\" class=\"ez-toc-pull-right ez-toc-btn ez-toc-btn-xs ez-toc-btn-default ez-toc-toggle\" aria-label=\"Toggle Table of Content\"><span class=\"ez-toc-js-icon-con\"><span class=\"\"><span class=\"eztoc-hide\" style=\"display:none;\">Toggle</span><span class=\"ez-toc-icon-toggle-span\"><svg style=\"fill: #999;color:#999\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"list-377408\" width=\"20px\" height=\"20px\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M6 6H4v2h2V6zm14 0H8v2h12V6zM4 11h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2zM4 16h2v2H4v-2zm16 0H8v2h12v-2z\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></svg><svg style=\"fill: #999;color:#999\" class=\"arrow-unsorted-368013\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10px\" height=\"10px\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" version=\"1.2\" baseProfile=\"tiny\"><path d=\"M18.2 9.3l-6.2-6.3-6.2 6.3c-.2.2-.3.4-.3.7s.1.5.3.7c.2.2.4.3.7.3h11c.3 0 .5-.1.7-.3.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7zM5.8 14.7l6.2 6.3 6.2-6.3c.2-.2.3-.5.3-.7s-.1-.5-.3-.7c-.2-.2-.4-.3-.7-.3h-11c-.3 0-.5.1-.7.3-.2.2-.3.5-.3.7s.1.5.3.7z\"/></svg></span></span></span></a></span></div><nav><ul class='ez-toc-list ez-toc-list-level-1 eztoc-toggle-hide-by-default' ><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-1\" href=\"#The_early_years\" >The early years</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-2\" href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/2/#Indian_music\" >Indian music</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-3\" href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/3/#The_solo_years\" >The solo years</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-4\" href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/4/#All_things_must_pass\" >All things must pass</a></li></ul></nav></div><h2><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"The_early_years\"></span>The early years<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2><p>Harrison was born on <a href=\"#/1943/02/25/george-harrison-born/\">25 February 1943</a> in the family home at 12 Arnold Grove, Wavertree, Liverpool.</p><p>His parents were Harold and Louise Harrison, who had roots in Ireland. They had three other children: Louise, Harry and Peter, all of whom were older than George.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/george-harrison/biography/&quot;}' id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-12 gallery-columns-2 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/george-harrison-baby_01/'><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"132\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison-baby_01-132x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison as a baby\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison-baby_01-132x200.jpg 132w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison-baby_01.jpg 246w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 132px) 100vw, 132px\" data-attachment-id=\"27829\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/george-harrison-baby_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison-baby_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"246,372\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison as a baby\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison-baby_01.jpg\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/40s_george-harrison_001_family/'><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"200\" height=\"159\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_001_family-200x159.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison with his family, 1940s\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_001_family-200x159.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_001_family.jpg 441w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"10656\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/40s_george-harrison_001_family/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_001_family.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"441,350\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison with his family, 1940s\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_001_family.jpg\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/40s_george-harrison_002_family-2/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTEyIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDExMiI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"112\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_002_family-200x112.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison and family, 1940s\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_002_family-200x112.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_002_family.jpg 500w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"8346\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/40s_george-harrison_002_family-2/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_002_family.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"500,279\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison and family, 1940s\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s_george-harrison_002_family.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/george-harrison-mother-sister-louise/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMTAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTEwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"110\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/50s_george-harrison_004-110x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison, his sister Louise and their mother Louise\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/50s_george-harrison_004-110x200.jpg 110w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/50s_george-harrison_004.jpg 233w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 110px) 100vw, 110px\" data-attachment-id=\"8359\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/george-harrison-mother-sister-louise/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/50s_george-harrison_004.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"233,423\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison, his sister Louise and their mother Louise\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/50s_george-harrison_004.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>In 1950 the family moved to 25 Upton Green in Speke. George went to school at Dovedale Road, where he passed his 11 Plus and gained a place at the Liverpool Institute for Boys, a local grammar school.</p><p>He attended the Institute between 1954 and 1959. Not an especially gifted child academically, Harrison struggled as a student and left without any qualifications. He had trouble relating to his teachers, and insisted on wearing tight jeans and long hair, much to his parents consternation.</p><p>In 1959 Harrison formed a skiffle group, The Rebels, with his brother Peter and a friend, Arthur Kelly. Harrison&#8217;s mother bought him a guitar for £3, and the group&#8217;s debut gig at the British Legion club in Speke earned them 10 shillings.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/george-harrison/biography/&quot;}' id='gallery-2' class='gallery galleryid-12 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/george-harrison_010/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzEiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTMxIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"131\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_010-131x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison playing the guitar, circa 1950\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_010-131x200.jpg 131w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_010-380x580.jpg 380w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_010.jpg 492w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 131px) 100vw, 131px\" data-attachment-id=\"9359\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/george-harrison_010/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_010.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"492,750\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"2\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison playing the guitar, circa 1950\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_010.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/58_quarrymen/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTM0IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzNCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"134\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/58_quarrymen-200x134.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Quarrymen and Dennis Littler, 8 March 1958\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/58_quarrymen-200x134.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/58_quarrymen-580x388.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/58_quarrymen.jpg 760w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"8362\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/58_quarrymen/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/58_quarrymen.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"760,509\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"3\" data-image-title=\"The Quarrymen and Dennis Littler, 8 March 1958\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/58_quarrymen.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/581220_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTMzIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzMyI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"133\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/581220_01-200x133.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"The Quarrymen, 20 December 1958\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/581220_01-200x133.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/581220_01-580x385.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/581220_01.jpg 760w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" data-attachment-id=\"8792\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/581220_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/581220_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"760,504\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"The Quarrymen, 20 December 1958\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/581220_01.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>Harrison considered becoming an apprentice engineer after leaving school, but music dominated his passions and he performed with a number of fledgling groups in Liverpool. In 1958 he met the Quarrymen, whose ranks included <a href=\"#/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul McCartney</a>, a friend of Harrison&#8217;s from the Institute.</p><p>Although Harrison was considered too young to join the group, he did fill in when their regular guitarist Eric Griffiths was unavailable. Eventually he was accepted as a full member, despite the reservations of the Quarrymen founder and leader, <a href=\"#/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a>.</p><blockquote><div><p>Paul introduced me to George and I had to make the decision whether to let George in. I listened to George play and said, &#8220;Play &#8216;Raunchy'&#8221; [a 1958 hit for saxophonist Bill Justis]. Then I said, &#8220;OK, you can come in.&#8221;</p><p>I couldn&#8217;t be bothered with him when he first came around. He used to follow me around like a bloody kid, hanging around all the time. He was a kid who played guitar and he was a friend of Paul&#8217;s which made it easier. It took me years to come around to him, to start considering him as an equal.</p></div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon</div><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/george-harrison/biography/&quot;}' id='gallery-3' class='gallery galleryid-12 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/george-harrison_011/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNDUiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTQ1IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"145\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_011-145x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison, Hamburg, 1960\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_011-145x200.jpg 145w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_011-419x580.jpg 419w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_011.jpg 542w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 145px) 100vw, 145px\" data-attachment-id=\"9360\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/george-harrison/george-harrison_011/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_011.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"542,750\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison, Hamburg, 1960\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/george-harrison_011.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/61-george-harrison-cavern_02/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM0IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"134\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_02-134x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison at the Cavern Club, Liverpool, 1961\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_02-134x200.jpg 134w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_02-389x580.jpg 389w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_02.jpg 430w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 134px) 100vw, 134px\" data-attachment-id=\"27495\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/61-george-harrison-cavern_02/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_02.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"430,641\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison at the Cavern Club, Liverpool, 1961\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_02.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/61-george-harrison-cavern_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNjIiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTYyIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"162\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_01-162x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"George Harrison at the Cavern Club, Liverpool, 1961\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_01-162x200.jpg 162w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_01-471x580.jpg 471w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_01.jpg 473w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 162px) 100vw, 162px\" data-attachment-id=\"27494\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1961-photos/61-george-harrison-cavern_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"473,583\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"George Harrison at the Cavern Club, Liverpool, 1961\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/61-george-harrison-cavern_01.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>The band became Johnny and the Moondogs, and later the Silver Beetles. Their first trip to Hamburg in August 1960 took place while Harrison was just 17, and the Reeperbahn, the red light district where they played, proved an educative experience: &#8220;Everybody around the district were homosexuals, transvestites, pimps and hookers and I was in the middle of that, aged 17,&#8221; he said.</p><p>The first trip ended in Harrison&#8217;s deportation for working under-age. When they returned in March 1961 The Beatles had become more assured as performers, and in June cut their first single, <a href=\"#/songs/my-bonnie/\">&#8216;My Bonnie&#8217;</a>, as the backing band for <a href=\"#/people/tony-sheridan/\">Tony Sheridan</a>. For this they were paid 300 marks with no royalties.</p><p>At the band&#8217;s first recording session for EMI, producer <a href=\"#/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a> tried to ease the band&#8217;s nerves by saying, &#8220;Let me know if there&#8217;s anything you don&#8217;t like&#8221;. &#8220;Well, for a start,&#8221; replied Harrison, &#8220;I don&#8217;t like your tie.&#8221; This led to a succession of jokes being cracked in the studio, which endeared the band to the EMI staff.</p><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></span> <a href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <a href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/3/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></a> <a href=\"#/people/george-harrison/biography/4/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></a></div>",
  "textContent": "Beatle people » George HarrisonEverybody dreams of being famous, rich and famous. Once you get rich and famous, you think, ‘This wasn’t it.’ And that made me go on to find out what it is. In the end, you’re trying to find God. That’s the result of not being satisfied. And it doesn’t matter how much money, or property, or whatever you’ve got, unless you’re happy in your heart, then that’s it. And unfortunately, you can never gain perfect happiness unless you’ve got that state of consciousness that enables that.George HarrisonPublished: 14 March 2008  | Last updated: 5 September 2025 Biography  Pages: 1 2 3 4 George Harrison was lead guitarist, songwriter and singer with The Beatles. Although often overshadowed by the partnership of John Lennon and Paul McCartney during the band&#8217;s lifetime, he emerged as a significant talent in his own right. Contents Toggle The early years Indian music The solo years All things must pass The early years Harrison was born on 25 February 1943 in the family home at 12 Arnold Grove, Wavertree, Liverpool. His parents were Harold and Louise Harrison, who had roots in Ireland. They had three other children: Louise, Harry and Peter, all of whom were older than George. In 1950 the family moved to 25 Upton Green in Speke. George went to school at Dovedale Road, where he passed his 11 Plus and gained a place at the Liverpool Institute for Boys, a local grammar school. He attended the Institute between 1954 and 1959. Not an especially gifted child academically, Harrison struggled as a student and left without any qualifications. He had trouble relating to his teachers, and insisted on wearing tight jeans and long hair, much to his parents consternation. In 1959 Harrison formed a skiffle group, The Rebels, with his brother Peter and a friend, Arthur Kelly. Harrison&#8217;s mother bought him a guitar for £3, and the group&#8217;s debut gig at the British Legion club in Speke earned them 10 shillings. Harrison considered becoming an apprentice engineer after leaving school, but music dominated his passions and he performed with a number of fledgling groups in Liverpool. In 1958 he met the Quarrymen, whose ranks included Paul McCartney , a friend of Harrison&#8217;s from the Institute. Although Harrison was considered too young to join the group, he did fill in when their regular guitarist Eric Griffiths was unavailable. Eventually he was accepted as a full member, despite the reservations of the Quarrymen founder and leader, John Lennon . Paul introduced me to George and I had to make the decision whether to let George in. I listened to George play and said, &#8220;Play &#8216;Raunchy'&#8221; [a 1958 hit for saxophonist Bill Justis]. Then I said, &#8220;OK, you can come in.&#8221; I couldn&#8217;t be bothered with him when he first came around. He used to follow me around like a bloody kid, hanging around all the time. He was a kid who played guitar and he was a friend of Paul&#8217;s which made it easier. It took me years to come around to him, to start considering him as an equal. John Lennon The band became Johnny and the Moondogs, and later the Silver Beetles. Their first trip to Hamburg in August 1960 took place while Harrison was just 17, and the Reeperbahn, the red light district where they played, proved an educative experience: &#8220;Everybody around the district were homosexuals, transvestites, pimps and hookers and I was in the middle of that, aged 17,&#8221; he said. The first trip ended in Harrison&#8217;s deportation for working under-age. When they returned in March 1961 The Beatles had become more assured as performers, and in June cut their first single, &#8216;My Bonnie&#8217; , as the backing band for Tony Sheridan . For this they were paid 300 marks with no royalties. At the band&#8217;s first recording session for EMI, producer George Martin tried to ease the band&#8217;s nerves by saying, &#8220;Let me know if there&#8217;s anything you don&#8217;t like&#8221;. &#8220;Well, for a start,&#8221; replied Harrison, &#8220;I don&#8217;t like your tie.&#8221; This led to a succession of jokes being cracked in the studio, which endeared the band to the EMI staff. Pages: 1 2 3 4 ",
